\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Initial states and required ansatz circuits for the three phases: (a) trivial; (b) topological; (c) AFM. The dashed box $U^{(k)}$ is the $k$th variational layer; $\theta ^{(k)}_j$ ($\varphi ^{(k)}_j$) is the $XX{+}YY$ ($ZZ$) angle shared by the $j$th mirror-symmetric bond orbit in layer $k$ (odd $O_j\leftrightarrow O_{M+1-j}$, even $E_j\leftrightarrow E_{M-j}$; $\theta =\varphi $ at $\delta =0$). Even-bond sublayer first in (a) and (c), odd-bond sublayer first in (b). }}{6}{}}
\newlabel{fig:D06}{{3}{6}{}{}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Cost functions at $p=1$ and the experiment--simulation comparison. (a),(b) Cost functions at $p=1$ versus $s$ for (a) $\delta =-2$ and (b) $\delta =0.85$: $E_0$ (exact, blue solid) with the three initial-state costs (triv green dashed, topo orange dotted, AFM black dashdot); background bands identify the initial-state branch minimizing the $p=1$ cost at each grid point; circles identify the branch with the lowest mean optimized cost within each interval. (c),(d) Combined quantity $Q$ for (c) $\delta =-2$ and (d) $\delta =0.85$: simulation $p=1$ (black) and $p=2$ (gray) fixed-scale curves with experimental window scatter ($p=1$, 16-unit window of the 500-unit round; colors indicate the lowest-energy initial-state branches in (a),(b)). }}{7}{}}
